--- !yfi/header
version: 1
namespace: edges::extends
visibility: public
--- !node &Alpha
pub port: 1
--- !node &Beta
pub port: 2
--- !node &Gamma
pub port: 3
# An **abstract edge** is a `!type` that declares `connections`. There is no
# second spelling for it: `!edge` is concrete exactly as `!node` is, and the
# abstract counterpart of a concrete node is a `!type`, whatever the node is.
--- !type &Relation
pub connections:
pub weight: !!int
# `connections` is one member, absorbed by the ordinary shallow, left-biased
# rule. Restating it replaces the sequence **whole**; extension never appends.
--- !edge &Owns
extends: Relation
pub connections: [Alpha, Beta]
pub weight: 3
# A family that fixes its endpoints once...
--- !type &Pair
extends: Relation
pub connections: [Alpha, Gamma]
pub weight: 1
# ...and a concrete edge that supplies none of its own, and has them anyway.
--- !edge &Inherits
extends: Pair
# An edge extending a family that declares neither of the language's own two
# members. `connections` is written by the language, not by the family, so it
# is never `W0301` — otherwise the compiler would report its own vocabulary as
# a misspelled field.
--- !type &Labelled
pub label: !!str untitled
--- !edge &Named
extends: Labelled
pub label: owns
pub connections: [Alpha, Beta]
pub definition:
  from: 0
  to: 1
